  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "HMT-01",
      "title": "Matrix size sufficient for a height moment",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-height-moments",
      "statement": "Each natural moment A is integrable on a finite-volume Haar fundamental domain for the arithmetic special linear group of each totally complex field, at every size N≥A+2. The form comparison uses A=2am with a selected for the field before N and m the degree. The proof then squares the coefficient bound and uses u≤u²+1 on this domain to take the mean.",
      "hypotheses": "The moment estimate requires a totally complex number field L′. Its use in the stable comparison additionally requires 1≤m<r₂(L′), a prime element π, the prescribed starting size, N≥3 and the threshold from the comparison of Hecke periods. A+2 is sufficient for the moment alone. Constants in chart/partition bounds and the integral may depend on field, size and data.",
      "definitions": [
        "height from primal/dual Hermitian minima on the integral lattice",
        "one complex matrix factor per infinite place",
        "partition growth exponent uniform in N",
        "moment exponent vs form degree vs matrix size"
      ],
