  "outstanding": [
    "CUP derives the finite cusp cover from adelic reduction and the determinant correction. The denominator and product-formula estimates in each place, adelic reduction and discreteness of the arithmetic group have their own suppliers. The threshold is sufficient; the endpoint moment is not decided by this estimate.",
    "FIN derives the flag angles and coercive inequality. CIN identifies the common invariant functions with constants almost everywhere, which puts each mean-zero coefficient in the complement where the gap applies. The partition of unity, central averaging and local evaluation of the periods use further results."
  ],
  "review_scope": "Compared the moment and common-cover gap calculations to the pinned source, with an independent review of the formulas, quantified matrix size, worked ray and cover-index cancellation. The source and example describe analytic inputs to the odd-dimensional rank argument."
}
